abstract: >-
  MATLAB code solving the full Euler equations of irrotational surface gravity waves over a bed of variable depth.
  The fluid layer is mapped conformally onto a strip, the bed under the waves is found by fixed-point iterations, and
  the evolution equations in conformal variables are solved by a Fourier pseudo-spectral method with an adaptive time
  integrator. Version 2.0.0 corrects the evolution equations of version 1.0, which were those of the published article
  (the elevation and the potential are now transported with one tangential velocity), the sign of the bed in the map,
  and the periodic extension of the bed, now a mirror image.
